@api @group-i
Feature: Archiving and unarchiving a collection cascades to its sub-content.

  Background:
    Given the following users:
      | Username       | Roles     |
      | John Moderator | moderator |
    And I am logged in as "John Moderator"

  Scenario: Archiving a collection archives its sub-content.
    Given the following "collection" content:
      | title      | state            |
      | Collection | archival_request |
    And the following "custom_page" content:
      | title         | collection | state     |
      | Custom page 1 | Collection | published |
      | Custom page 2 | Collection | draft     |
    And the following "news" content:
      | title  | collection | state     |
      | News 1 | Collection | published |
      | News 2 | Collection | draft     |
    And the "group_archive_related_content" queue is empty
    When I go to the edit form of the "Collection" collection
    And I fill in "Motivation" with "Archiving collection."
    And I press "Archive"
    Then I should see the following success messages:
      | Success messages                                                            |
      | The archiving process of the Collection has been initiated.                 |
      | You will receive an email notification as soon as the process is completed. |
    And the number of items in the "group_archive_related_content" queue should be 1

    # Execute the queue.
    Given I run the "group_archive_related_content" queue worker
    Then the number of items in the "group_archive_related_content" queue should be 0
    And the workflow state of the "Custom page 1" content should be "archived"
    And the workflow state of the "Custom page 2" content should be "draft"
    And the workflow state of the "News 1" content should be "archived"
    And the workflow state of the "News 2" content should be "draft"

  Scenario: Unarchiving a collection unarchives its sub-content but leaves its solutions archived.
    Given the following "collection" content:
      | title          | state     |
      | Sample Cluster | published |
    And the following "solution" content:
      | title        | collection     | state     |
      | Cluster Soln | Sample Cluster | published |
    And the workflow state of the "Cluster Soln" content is changed to "archived"
    And the following "news" content:
      | title          | collection     | state     |
      | Cluster News 1 | Sample Cluster | published |
      | Cluster News 2 | Sample Cluster | draft     |
    And the workflow state of the "Cluster News 1" content is changed to "archived"
    And the following "custom_page" content:
      | title          | collection     | state     |
      | Cluster Page 1 | Sample Cluster | published |
    And the workflow state of the "Cluster Page 1" content is changed to "archived"
    # Bring the collection into the archived state to set up the precondition.
    And the workflow state of the "Sample Cluster" content is changed to "archived"
    # Clear the queue items generated by the archival setup above, so that only
    # the unarchive transition under test is asserted below.
    And the "group_archive_related_content" queue is empty
    When I go to the edit form of the "Sample Cluster" collection
    Then I should see the button "Unarchive"
    When I press "Unarchive"
    Then I should see the following success messages:
      | Success messages                                              |
      | The unarchiving process of the Collection has been initiated. |
    And the number of items in the "group_archive_related_content" queue should be 1

    # Execute the queue.
    Given I run the "group_archive_related_content" queue worker
    Then the number of items in the "group_archive_related_content" queue should be 0
    And the workflow state of the "Sample Cluster" content should be "published"
    And the workflow state of the "Cluster News 1" content should be "published"
    And the workflow state of the "Cluster News 2" content should be "draft"
    And the workflow state of the "Cluster Page 1" content should be "published"
    # Solutions keep their own archive lifecycle, so they stay archived.
    And the workflow state of the "Cluster Soln" content should be "archived"

    When I go to the homepage of the "Sample Cluster" collection
    Then I should not see the text "Archived" in the "Header"
